course: dictionary
lesson: 3290
title: Essential: the things you really need
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Essential means completely necessary. You cannot manage without it. Water is essential for living things, because a plant or an animal will not survive without it.
explain: Read this sentence: «Bailiffs can collect money owed only after a court decision and many warnings, under strict rules, and cannot take essentials.» The clue is the last part: bailiffs cannot take essentials. The law would not let them take things people really need, so essentials must mean things like food, water and warm clothes.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «A first-aid kit is essential on a trip» becomes «A first-aid kit is completely necessary on a trip.» That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Essential can also mean the most basic and important part of something. The bare essentials are the very basic things you need to get by. If you can say the bare essentials, you can always pick out what matters most.
fact: Essential means completely necessary; you cannot manage without it.
fact: Essentials are the things you really need, like food, water and warm clothes.
fact: In science, water, food, air and shelter are essential for living things.
fact: «Essential oils» are strong-smelling oils taken from plants.
fact: In maths, the essential information in a word problem is the part you need to solve it.
exercise: «Bailiffs cannot take essentials.» What are essentials? | Old, broken things | Toys and games | Things you want to buy for fun | *Things you really need, like food and warm clothes
exercise: «Water is essential for living things.» What does essential mean here? | *Completely necessary | Sometimes useful | Very cold | Optional, nice to have
exercise: «Pack only the bare essentials for the trip.» What are the bare essentials? | Things you have never used | *The most basic things you really need | Your favourite clothes for a party | A huge bag of sweets
test: «A first-aid kit is essential on a trip.» What does essential mean? | *Completely necessary | Something you may use for fun | Expensive | Only for adults
test: «It is essential that everyone wears a helmet when cycling.» What does it mean? | It is optional, so you can choose | It means the helmet is blue | It is a funny idea | *It is very important and necessary
exam: Which of these is essential for a person to stay alive? | *Water | A gold ring | A glossy magazine | A video game
